        "created_at": "2015-04-24T00:32:36.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I seem to remember seeing specific rules on when to reshuffle the trash upon emptying a deck, but I can't seem to find them anymore.</p><p>1) Do I reshuffle the trash when I need to \"reveal\" cards from an empty deck?</p><p>2) Do I reshuffle when I'm asked to \"discard\" from an empty deck?</p><p>3) If my deck becomes empty, do I reshuffle immediately, or do I wait until I need to draw/reveal/discard from that deck?</p><p>I know this sounds nitpicky, but I've been in situations where it matters. Like, \"Reveal cards until X equipment is found,\" when there's only 1 Equipment card left in the deck and I know I'd have to reshuffle the trash to get enough to fulfill the card.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Oh, and in a related question, when asked to generally put a card from the trash back into a deck, or in play (say, from Simulation Room, placing a villain target from trash into play), how do I choose which card to place? Do I take the most recently discarded/destroyed target? Choose randomly? Or put in whichever one the players agree to put in?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thanks!</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:36.365Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
